course: dictionary
lesson: 13575
title: Incapable and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Incapable means you cannot do something because you do not have the ability or power to do it. «The little puppy was incapable of opening the gate.» The puppy is too small and weak to do it, so the clue is the puppy's size. Notice that incapable is often followed by of and a doing word ending in -ing.
explain: Sometimes incapable describes a person who cannot look after themselves, for example because of illness. «After her operation, Grandma was incapable of getting out of bed alone.» The clue is that she needs help, so she cannot manage on her own.
explain: In everyday talk, calling someone incapable can sound rude, as if they are useless at something. «Tom is completely incapable of cooking, so Dad always makes dinner.» Ask yourself: is the word being kind or unkind? Then you will know how it feels.
fact: Incapable means not able to do something.
fact: «Incapable of» is followed by a doing word ending in -ing, like «incapable of swimming».
fact: «Incapable» can also mean not able to look after yourself, for example because of illness.
fact: «Incapable» can sound rude when it is used about a person, so use it carefully.
fact: The opposite of incapable is capable: «capable» means able to do something.
exercise: «The robot was incapable of climbing stairs.» What does incapable mean here? | Happy to watch others climb | *Not able to climb them | Quick at climbing | Excited to climb them
exercise: Grandma was incapable of looking after herself after her illness. What does incapable mean here? | *Not able to look after herself | Ready to go on holiday | Too clever for her own good | Able to look after the whole street
exercise: Find and copy one word that means the opposite of incapable. | *capable | silly | sleepy | hopeless
test: «Without his glasses, Sam was almost incapable of reading the sign.» What does this tell you? | *Sam was unable to read it well | Sam liked the sign a lot | Sam wrote the sign himself | Sam read it very quickly
test: Why might someone be upset to be called incapable? | Because it means they are the best at a game | *Because it can sound as if they are useless at something | Because it is a happy word | Because it means they are very clever
exam: Which sentence uses incapable correctly? | The baby incapable was a big red ball. | The baby was incapable to the park happily. | *The baby was incapable of walking yet. | Incapable the baby walked to the shop.
